{
  "version": 1,
  "id": "opf-script-corpora-v1",
  "description": "Script-specific shaping corpora for the open script-replacement faces (RR-17, FF-44). One group per ISO 15924 script that the OPF language catalog, the font-scheme catalog and the renderer's script slots use. Each sample exercises one shaping behaviour (joining, ligatures, marks, conjuncts, vowel placement, stacking, tone marks, digits, punctuation, bidi, mixed Latin, text without spaces) and is run through every open face that serves its script.",
  "provenance": "Original text written for OPF for this corpus, kept to short phrases, common words (days, months, numerals, language and country names, greetings) and the catalog's own font-scheme sample strings; no third-party prose is copied. Words are chosen to hit a shaping behaviour, not to carry meaning; the corpus does not claim editorial or translation quality. Public-domain proverbs and the catalog's own samples are marked in `source`.",
  "license": "MIT (same as the repository)",
  "groups": [
